    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d504">

                <pb facs="1077" n="1037" xml:id="pg1037"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">262A.84A41/10–1752: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 504<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Embassy in
                        Lebanon</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d504-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1952-10-22T18:05:00-05:00">October 22, 1952—6:05
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>769. Re Embtel 679 Oct 3 and 798 Oct
                        17.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d504-f2"/> Dept well aware growing Arab preference
                    interpret Bonn–Israel agreement as being imposed on Germans by US. If US
                    protests too much, Arabs feel their suspicions confirmed (Beirut 656 Sept 30)
                    but silence also can be interpreted as sign guilt.</p>
                <p>Dept suggests that on all appropriate occasions NE
                    Missions might try divert Arab attn by stressing (1) successful conclusion Bonn
                    agreement underscores and makes more feasible Israel’s obligation for Pal
                    refugee compensation; (2) successful efforts PCC
                    on Israel release blocked Arab accounts; (3) PCC
                    progress with Israel on determination of Arab property losses.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bruce</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d504-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d504-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated to Amman, Cairo, Baghdad, Damascus, and Bonn.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d504-f2" n="2" xml:id="d504-f2-content">
                <p>Neither printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
